@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title 11. Security Model (Current Source)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

rectangle "Input/Prompt Security" {
  [HttpChatController\n(unrestricted)] as HttpController
  [Product/Reservation/Search Controllers\n(scoped)] as ScopedControllers
  [PromptInjectionGuard] as PromptGuard
  [HumanMessageService] as HumanMsg
}

rectangle "Tool Call Security" {
  [McpToolExecutionService] as ToolExec
  [McpProperties allowlist] as AllowList
  [AgentScope\n(allowedServers/allowedToolsByServer)] as AgentScope
  [URL/Host Validator] as UrlValidator
}

rectangle "Error Safety" {
  [GlobalExceptionHandler] as ErrorHandler
  [ChatProcessingException] as ChatException
}

HttpController --> PromptGuard : sanitize user/tool text
ScopedControllers --> PromptGuard : sanitize user/tool text
ToolExec --> AllowList : server/tool allow check
ToolExec --> AgentScope : scope enforcement
ToolExec --> UrlValidator : block localhost/internal/private host
ToolExec --> HumanMsg : fallback message path
ErrorHandler --> ChatException : map to safe ErrorResponse

note right of PromptGuard
Protect against prompt injection attempts
- sanitize user input
- sanitize tool raw payload
end note

note right of ToolExec
SSRF guardrails
- http/https only
- block localhost/internal domains
- block private/loopback/link-local IP
end note

note bottom of ErrorHandler
Do not expose internal details
- stack trace
- secrets/token
- raw MCP payload
end note

@enduml
